       - "2026-10-18: graphics-remaster step A0 (cut and baseline, plan section 5 A0): the branch is cut at 026133b with the integration plan on top (0779350). F10 and F11 are in their narrowed form in code and in game (a fresh user dir boots to 4x MSAA at render scale 1; with no spawned unit the shadow depth map holds the trees and bushes). Gate tags 425/425 ([graphics] 378/379, the known DDS fixture case), smoke 3/3 with KHR_debug ids 131169, 131154 and 131218 only. New look baseline 20261017-233303-gr-base; a second boot of the same build shows the Sinai ground band, the crew views and the fire and smoke views are not repeatable between boots, so pixel-exact checks use the other views. Quiet-GPU timing at 1080p, render scale 1.0, 4x MSAA on the RTX 4060 Ti (20 hero views, 3 interleaved rounds): Remastered takes 2.0 to 11.9 ms of GPU time on 17 views and 17.4 to 24.3 ms on the long views (sunrise_ridge, valley 05:15, Eden broken_high, 10,800 to 12,900 draws). There the GPU span is set by draw submission rather than shading (the 26 to 31 ms CPU frame is longer than the GPU span; 54 to 73% GPU utilisation at P0; Classic costs the same on sunrise_ridge, 18.10 against 17.41 ms), and MENU's 2.5 to 7.5 ms base frame was measured after the frame-cost fixes (step A4), so the B steps judge headroom on those views only after A4. Sky and sea views run mostly at P3 or P5 clocks, so the timing gate now logs the GPU clock with every shot. No engine change."
       - "2026-10-18: graphics-remaster step A1 (switches, gates, tooling, plan section 5 A1): one registry (Graphics/Remaster/FeatureSwitches) holds every triSetLighting key, the 26 feature switches of plan 3.1 (all on, all inert until their step lands) and the new mode word baseline (every switch off); FeatureGates decides per frame whether an enabled feature can show (low sun, night, wet, local or combat light, clouds; gates=0 forces them on); the dev overlay's Lighting tab is generated from the registry with a Features section showing each gate; triFeatureState logs switches and gates with every capture shot; triSetFixedStep fixes the simulation step and P-mode pairs hold (two paused renders of a fire are pixel-identical); triPinCloudDrift holds the cloud shadows and sky clouds, which do not follow the pinned clock. Capture tooling in the repo: features_ab (16 hero views, off then on, fixed clocks), banddiff.py, the A0 timing rig (run-timing.ps1, gpu_sampler.ps1, summarize_timing.py, gen_timing.py) and the video skeleton (capture_motion.sqf, gen_video_tests.py with every 7.3 row, make_video.py). No pixel changes: horizon and ground bands match the A0 build within noise; timing on the long views matches A0 at P0 (sunrise_ridge 17.31 against 17.41 ms). Unit gate 452/452 (27 new), smoke 3/3."
       - "2026-10-18: graphics-remaster step A2 (shader split and shared tables, plan section 5 A2): the remastered fragment prelude is ten pieces by concern (header, LitConstants, inputs, shadows, terrain and clouds, sky, local lights, surface, shade, finish; sky, lights and surface in EngineGL33_LightingShaders{Sky,Lights,Surface}.cpp) joined by one table; the LitConstants block is one string with no copies; the post GLSL moved to EngineGL33_PostShaders.cpp (no GL code, so the unit tests link it) with a kPostShaders table and s_glslPostCommon (AO's depth reconstruction); the slots planned for later features (LitConstPlanned 58 to 78) and the texture unit table (units 6, 8 to 15 allocated, one static_assert, kLitSamplers binds every lit sampler, shadow unit named kShadowMapUnit) are fixed. No pixel changes: every assembled program (8 remastered, 7 post, 15 classic) is byte for byte the tip's, checked with glsl_extract.py --dump and with the engine's own accessors; features_ab on the A2 build is pixel-identical to the A1 build on the five repeatable views and within the same-config noise on the others; timing at P0 within -0.27 to +0.18 ms of A1. Tests go through the accessors (4 new cases: every raw GLSL string reaches a program, the assembly tables the lab reads, the concern of each piece, the unit table); five contract mutations each turn their case red. Unit gate 456/456, smoke 3/3. The lighting lab assembles the same programs (glsl_extract load_programs) and decodes git output as UTF-8."
+      - "2026-10-18: graphics-remaster step A3 (post stages, plan section 5 A3): the post pass is a fixed list of thirteen stages (Graphics/Remaster/PostStages: resolve, linear depth, tag readout, AO, reflections, air, bloom, shafts, combat scatter, composite, TAA resolve, sharpen, debug view), every planned stage holding its place and GPU mark, seven landed; PlanPostStages decides per frame which stages run (the early return asks every stage, with the old meaning: a knob that is on keeps the pass) and EndWorldScene runs them on one PostFrame, each followed by its own timestamp. New PostLinearDepth: half-resolution R32F view depth, nearest and farthest of each 2x2 on a checkerboard, the sky at 1e6; it feeds nothing yet, so it runs only for the new linear depth debug view (debug=5), 0.01 ms at P0. No pixel changes: the 30 existing programs are byte-identical, features_ab is pixel-identical to the A2 build on the five repeatable views and the three-island set within boot noise. The new GPU sections show the MSAA resolve (0.22 to 0.65 ms at P0), not AO (0.06 to 0.20 ms), is the largest fixed post cost; frame medians at P0 within -0.22 to +0.27 ms of A2. Unit gate 466/466 (10 new), seven contract mutations red, smoke 3/3."
